  "reasoning": "The case involves two distinct criminal conduct areas. First, the teaching and research center (a public institution) received a kickback of 10% from a book supplier, which was hidden in an off‑books petty cash fund. This constitutes the crime of unit bribery (单位受贿罪). As the director and legal representative of the unit, Yue also personally participated in the illicit handling of the money, which meets the elements of personal bribery (受贿罪). Second, Yue was found to have a blood alcohol concentration of 266.64 mg/100 ml while driving, which is well above the legal limit and therefore constitutes the crime of dangerous driving (危险驾驶罪). All three offenses are separate crimes, so they should be listed together, separated by semicolons.",
